# component: chart
# decisions: DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-9
# hunks:
#   FOC-1: `[&_.recharts-surface]:outline-hidden` becomes
#     `[&_.recharts-surface:not(:focus-visible)]:outline-hidden`. MEASURED, not assumed:
#     recharts' `accessibilityLayer` (default `true` since 3.9.2) renders the ROOT `<svg>` — the
#     element carrying `.recharts-surface` — with `role="application"` and `tabIndex={0}`, so the
#     chart is a keyboard-reachable control. `outline-hidden` compiles to
#     `--tw-outline-style: none` ON THAT ELEMENT, and every outline utility including
#     `base.css`'s global `:focus-visible` resolves `outline-style: var(--tw-outline-style)`, so
#     upstream's unscoped reset silently defeats the one focus affordance on the one element the
#     component made focusable. The reset still applies at rest, which is all it was ever for.
#     This is an UPSTREAM DEFECT fixed under an existing row, not a new decision. FLAGGED FOR MK,
#     and worth reporting to shadcn. `chart.test.tsx` asserts the focused surface paints.
#   FOC-9: `[&_svg:focus-visible]:-outline-offset-2` — the plot fills the surface edge to edge,
#     so the outward `outline-offset: 1px` would be drawn over the chart's own frame. FOC-9 is
#     the one permitted local deviation, and it moves the offset ONLY.
#   Nothing else. `ChartTooltipContent`'s `shadow-xl`, `border-border/50` and `rounded-lg`, and
#     the `#ccc`/`#fff` attribute selectors that retarget recharts' hard-coded defaults, are
#     upstream's verbatim — BRD-1, BRD-4 and DOC-10 all resolve as **shadcn**, and the two hex
#     literals are recharts' own values being MATCHED in a selector, not colours being authored,
#     which is why `design-lint`'s `hex-color` rule reads them in an attribute-selector position
#     and upstream's own file is what defines them. `--chart-1…8` and `--chart-single` are
#     untouched by this file: the palette is the token layer's (MK 2026-09-18, Batch 1), and
#     upstream's chart blocks name `--chart-1…5`, which keep working.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
